On Sunday afternoon I sit on the sofa in my living room.
The sun is shining through the window, and the room is beautifully bright.
I have my computer on the table in front of me for a long video call.
My whole family in Mexico is on the screen.
I can see my parents, my sister Sofía, and my brother Diego.
Suddenly our dog, Lola, barks very loudly.
She jumps excitedly around in front of the camera.
"Lola misses you," Sofía says and laughs.
"I miss you all too," I say and wave to them.
My father asks about my job and my everyday life here.
I tell them about my work, my badminton, and my sweet neighbor.
We talk together for over an hour.
I look around my bright living room.
I look at the nice green plant from yesterday.
A lot of time has passed since January.
"Are you happy living there?" my mother asks.
I smile broadly at her.
"Yes," I answer.
"I truly feel at home in the city now."
